1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
iso

2
00:00:04,040 --> 00:00:10,920
ゆさしいひだまりにチャイムがディレイする

3
00:00:11,920 --> 00:00:18,540
頬を撫でる風 i buki は深くなってく

4
00:00:19,740 --> 00:00:24,940
とおまわりのなみだ なまえつけた明日

5
00:00:24,940 --> 00:00:54,920
Thank you.

6
00:00:54,940 --> 00:01:08,720
Hey, after you met Kurumi, you decided you wanted to become cuter, right?

7
00:01:09,800 --> 00:01:13,200
Think very carefully about why you wanted that in the first place.

8
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:21,080
Happy birthday, Sawako.

9
00:01:24,940 --> 00:01:54,920
Happy birthday, Sawako.

10
00:01:54,920 --> 00:01:56,060
...isn't here yet.

11
00:01:58,580 --> 00:01:59,720
Yano and Yoshida?

12
00:02:00,800 --> 00:02:02,000
They're not coming.

13
00:02:04,800 --> 00:02:06,920
And Sanada isn't...

14
00:02:07,920 --> 00:02:08,460
...either.

15
00:02:08,460 --> 00:02:26,240
Well, let's go.

16
00:02:26,240 --> 00:02:27,860
It's okay.

17
00:02:27,860 --> 00:02:31,460
What's this mean?

18
00:02:31,460 --> 00:02:32,120
...

19
00:02:32,120 --> 00:03:02,100
Thank you.

20
00:03:02,120 --> 00:03:09,120
He won't... look back at me.

21
00:03:09,120 --> 00:03:28,120
But... I can't look at him either... for some reason.

22
00:03:28,120 --> 00:03:35,120
Watch out!

23
00:03:35,120 --> 00:03:36,120
Oh...

24
00:03:36,120 --> 00:03:42,120
Too close!

25
00:03:42,120 --> 00:03:49,120
Careful... these steps are... made of stone.

26
00:03:49,120 --> 00:03:57,120
Oh, right! I didn't even notice because they were buried under all that snow! It's almost like they were invisible!

27
00:03:57,120 --> 00:04:12,120
Are you kidding me right now? What the heck are those two even doing? How frustrating!

28
00:04:12,120 --> 00:04:17,120
Jisoo, call him. You got it!

29
00:04:17,120 --> 00:04:22,120
You changed where we were gonna meet up, but you never said we'd have to hide in a bush.

30
00:04:22,120 --> 00:04:24,120
Shhh! Real quiet!

31
00:04:24,120 --> 00:04:30,120
Uh...

32
00:04:30,120 --> 00:04:31,120
Hello?

33
00:04:31,120 --> 00:04:33,120
Hey, Kasihaya! It's Jisoo!

34
00:04:33,120 --> 00:04:38,120
Huh? Where are you? Yoshida?

35
00:04:38,120 --> 00:04:42,120
Huh? That's Jisoo? Your voice is too loud!

36
00:04:42,120 --> 00:04:43,120
Oops! I'm so sorry!

37
00:04:43,120 --> 00:04:44,120
I'm so sorry!

38
00:04:44,120 --> 00:04:49,120
So, we ended up not being able to go at the last minute. I hope you can forgive us!

39
00:04:49,120 --> 00:04:55,120
Total coincidence, but apparently Ryu got busy too. Anyway, he told me to give you both his regards.

40
00:04:55,120 --> 00:04:56,120
Huh?

41
00:04:56,120 --> 00:05:00,120
Well, uh, just be sure to make a lot of wishes for the rest of us, alright?

42
00:05:00,120 --> 00:05:05,120
Uh, okay. Sure. Did I imagine that?

43
00:05:05,120 --> 00:05:11,120
By the way, we already told Sawako about it. Kinda sprang it on her.

44
00:05:11,120 --> 00:05:16,120
So, there's a possibility she's still a little flustered from that.

45
00:05:16,120 --> 00:05:21,120
Take good care of her for us, Kasihaya. Okay?

46
00:05:21,120 --> 00:05:23,120
Hm.

47
00:05:25,120 --> 00:05:30,120
That was Yoshida who called. She apologized for having to ditch last minute.

48
00:05:30,120 --> 00:05:35,120
Uh... That's right. I never explained anything to him.

49
00:05:37,120 --> 00:05:40,120
I see. They covered that part for me.

50
00:05:44,120 --> 00:05:46,120
Are you feeling cold?

51
00:05:46,120 --> 00:05:47,120
Huh?

52
00:05:48,120 --> 00:05:51,120
There's still lots of time until midnight comes around.

53
00:05:51,120 --> 00:05:54,120
They're passing out hot Hamazake over there. Come on.

54
00:05:54,120 --> 00:05:56,120
Uh...

55
00:05:56,120 --> 00:05:58,120
Ah.

56
00:05:58,120 --> 00:06:25,240
He's beside me.

57
00:06:28,120 --> 00:06:39,700
Yes, they finally started walking side-by-side, and now they're on their way to go get some amazake.

58
00:06:40,180 --> 00:06:42,040
Hey, let's get there before them!

59
00:06:42,620 --> 00:06:44,100
That's what this is about.

60
00:06:44,840 --> 00:06:46,040
Are you two for real?

61
00:06:46,840 --> 00:06:49,660
After Shota and I discuss plans, too.

62
00:06:51,580 --> 00:06:53,540
Now things are starting to get interesting.

63
00:06:53,800 --> 00:06:55,700
And this is only the beginning, Chizu.

64
00:06:55,700 --> 00:06:56,860
Oh, whatever.

65
00:06:56,860 --> 00:06:58,680
I just want amazake.

66
00:07:02,820 --> 00:07:04,960
There's always an idiot somewhere.

67
00:07:05,300 --> 00:07:06,100
Hold on.

68
00:07:06,860 --> 00:07:08,280
I think that's Joe.

69
00:07:10,020 --> 00:07:11,520
Yeah, you're right.

70
00:07:11,940 --> 00:07:13,900
He's a disgrace to our class.

71
00:07:14,740 --> 00:07:16,220
It's kind of weird.

72
00:07:16,680 --> 00:07:19,260
You mean how he looks just like his parents?

73
00:07:19,760 --> 00:07:20,520
Amazake.

74
00:07:20,520 --> 00:07:21,080
Wait.

75
00:07:21,460 --> 00:07:21,960
Oh, no.

76
00:07:22,260 --> 00:07:23,380
Sooko and Kazahaya.

77
00:07:25,040 --> 00:07:25,560
Crap.

78
00:07:25,900 --> 00:07:27,980
At this rate, Joe's going to catch sight of them.

79
00:07:28,280 --> 00:07:28,940
You're right.

80
00:07:29,420 --> 00:07:33,080
Joe loves Kazahaya, so I bet anything he'll be able to find him in no time.

81
00:07:33,180 --> 00:07:33,880
This is bad.

82
00:07:34,140 --> 00:07:34,700
Let's hurry.

83
00:07:34,700 --> 00:07:36,780
I bet the amazake.

84
00:07:36,880 --> 00:07:37,460
Come on, Ryu.

85
00:07:38,600 --> 00:07:40,260
It's so nice and toasty.

86
00:07:48,260 --> 00:07:50,520
What was that?

87
00:07:51,640 --> 00:07:53,300
Wow, look at his and Joe.

88
00:07:54,300 --> 00:07:55,740
Wow, what a coincidence.

89
00:07:56,600 --> 00:07:56,860
Huh?

90
00:07:57,040 --> 00:07:57,460
What the?

91
00:07:58,080 --> 00:07:59,360
Did you guys come together?

92
00:08:00,180 --> 00:08:01,480
Invite me to Ryu?

93
00:08:01,860 --> 00:08:02,560
Hey, Joe.

94
00:08:02,660 --> 00:08:03,740
Who are you here with?

95
00:08:03,840 --> 00:08:05,060
Oh, just my parents.

96
00:08:05,600 --> 00:08:06,020
Really?

97
00:08:06,360 --> 00:08:07,880
What about your usual crew?

98
00:08:08,460 --> 00:08:10,740
At home, watching comedies and stuff like that?

99
00:08:11,020 --> 00:08:11,460
Good.

100
00:08:11,880 --> 00:08:13,320
No one else to interfere, then.

101
00:08:13,320 --> 00:08:16,580
Uh, so where's Kazahaya?

102
00:08:17,780 --> 00:08:22,080
Because, like, I'm pretty sure I saw him walking around here just before you guys came up to me.

103
00:08:23,120 --> 00:08:24,700
Uh, that's weird.

104
00:08:24,860 --> 00:08:28,300
He actually couldn't make it, so you must have seen someone who looks similar to him.

105
00:08:28,360 --> 00:08:29,580
You really think so?

106
00:08:29,660 --> 00:08:30,460
Just drop it!

107
00:08:30,660 --> 00:08:31,780
Even if he was here!

108
00:08:32,080 --> 00:08:33,840
Don't you think he'd be hanging out with us?

109
00:08:35,300 --> 00:08:36,700
She's holding my arm.

110
00:08:37,520 --> 00:08:38,080
You're right!

111
00:08:38,740 --> 00:08:41,660
No way it was him, because the girl on that guy's arm was too cute!

112
00:08:41,660 --> 00:08:44,840
Hmm, good thing he's an idiot.

113
00:08:45,980 --> 00:08:48,980
Maybe, Yano has a secret crush on me!

114
00:08:49,460 --> 00:08:50,580
I want Amazake.

115
00:08:58,080 --> 00:08:59,000
They're gone!

116
00:08:59,400 --> 00:08:59,800
Success!

117
00:09:00,580 --> 00:09:02,660
Sweet, my arm might touch her boobs!

118
00:09:02,660 --> 00:09:04,880
You better not be trying to cop a feel!

119
00:09:10,160 --> 00:09:10,800
Hmm?

120
00:09:11,660 --> 00:09:15,560
From the fire.

121
00:09:15,880 --> 00:09:17,600
Now I feel all warm and cozy.

122
00:09:18,440 --> 00:09:21,140
Amazake sounds really good right now, doesn't it, guys?

123
00:09:22,020 --> 00:09:24,260
Actually, I don't like Amazake.

124
00:09:25,400 --> 00:09:26,860
Nah, that stuff totally sucks.

125
00:09:27,220 --> 00:09:28,920
Aw, now that's sad.

126
00:09:30,400 --> 00:09:30,960
Amazake.

127
00:09:30,960 --> 00:09:40,020
We've got hot drinks.

128
00:09:40,340 --> 00:09:42,040
They'll warm you right up.

129
00:09:43,480 --> 00:09:44,920
Anyone want Amazake?

130
00:09:46,920 --> 00:09:48,060
Amazake here.

131
00:09:48,400 --> 00:09:49,600
Come get some.

132
00:09:49,600 --> 00:09:52,380
Are you interested?

133
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:54,780
It's really tasty.

134
00:09:55,660 --> 00:09:56,620
Uh, two, please.

135
00:09:56,620 --> 00:09:59,360
Two cups for the young couple.

136
00:10:00,020 --> 00:10:00,340
Huh?

137
00:10:00,840 --> 00:10:01,380
Couple?

138
00:10:01,380 --> 00:10:01,500
Couple?

139
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:08,720
Here.

140
00:10:10,160 --> 00:10:12,080
Oh, thanks so much.

141
00:10:12,080 --> 00:10:17,760
What do I do?

142
00:10:18,020 --> 00:10:19,700
I'm unexpectedly...

143
00:10:20,700 --> 00:10:21,200
Happy.

144
00:10:21,200 --> 00:10:24,740
S-Stop it, Sawaka.

145
00:10:25,100 --> 00:10:26,740
It was just a misunderstanding.

146
00:10:28,020 --> 00:10:30,640
I hope Kazehaya didn't mind her saying that.

147
00:10:31,740 --> 00:10:32,940
Is he upset?

148
00:10:33,480 --> 00:10:35,460
Ah, it's so warm.

149
00:10:35,460 --> 00:10:41,100
I'm probably the only one who cared about it.

150
00:10:41,780 --> 00:10:43,020
Oh, that's embarrassing.

151
00:10:47,920 --> 00:10:48,800
It's good.

152
00:10:49,360 --> 00:10:49,720
Oh, yeah?

153
00:10:58,040 --> 00:10:59,060
You're so right.

154
00:10:59,380 --> 00:11:01,960
This is the first time that Amazake actually tasted good.

155
00:11:01,960 --> 00:11:06,920
You don't like Amazake?

156
00:11:08,400 --> 00:11:10,640
I've never really been the biggest fan of it.

157
00:11:11,400 --> 00:11:12,920
Oh, I didn't know that.

158
00:11:15,500 --> 00:11:16,520
I'm happy.

159
00:11:17,460 --> 00:11:21,560
I've always wanted to see the sides of Kazehaya I never knew about.

160
00:11:22,640 --> 00:11:27,080
I was here to witness you experience something for the very first time.

161
00:11:27,080 --> 00:11:34,740
I've always wanted to see the sides of Kazehaya that no one knew about.

162
00:11:39,420 --> 00:11:42,720
But you've seen a few of those now.

163
00:11:43,360 --> 00:11:43,700
Huh?

164
00:11:44,580 --> 00:11:47,420
This is my first time going to a shrine on New Year's Eve.

165
00:11:48,380 --> 00:11:49,700
With just one person.

166
00:11:51,460 --> 00:11:55,420
And not to mention, it was the first time I ever bought a girl's cell phone strap.

167
00:11:55,420 --> 00:11:59,000
Oh, and there's one more.

168
00:12:03,200 --> 00:12:05,960
I'm wearing my first belly warmer today.

169
00:12:09,640 --> 00:12:11,840
I put a heating pad in the built-in pocket.

170
00:12:12,500 --> 00:12:14,340
And now my belly is nice and warm.

171
00:12:14,940 --> 00:12:17,540
Wait, that was supposed to be for my...

172
00:12:17,540 --> 00:12:18,440
Don't say it.

173
00:12:18,860 --> 00:12:21,020
Because I'm not giving it back.

174
00:12:21,020 --> 00:12:29,580
I really wish I'd been able to actually give Kazehaya the hat I knitted for him.

175
00:12:30,800 --> 00:12:33,380
No, it didn't have to be that hat.

176
00:12:36,260 --> 00:12:38,660
Something that I made just for Kazehaya.

177
00:12:39,440 --> 00:12:42,020
Or something that I chose specifically for him.

178
00:12:42,020 --> 00:12:44,760
That's what I really wanted to give him.

179
00:12:47,560 --> 00:12:49,240
He may have accepted it.

180
00:12:50,700 --> 00:12:52,020
And maybe even...

181
00:12:52,720 --> 00:12:53,400
Used it.

182
00:12:59,400 --> 00:12:59,960
So...

183
00:12:59,960 --> 00:13:01,640
Do you have an email address yet?

184
00:13:01,940 --> 00:13:02,800
Oh, uh...

185
00:13:02,800 --> 00:13:03,320
I do.

186
00:13:03,320 --> 00:13:05,500
Can I send you a message?

187
00:13:08,180 --> 00:13:09,760
I'll send one to you right now.

188
00:13:10,020 --> 00:13:11,900
Oh, but it's my first time doing it.

189
00:13:12,140 --> 00:13:13,580
So it might take me a little while.

190
00:13:14,580 --> 00:13:15,140
Wha...

191
00:13:15,140 --> 00:13:24,620
That's fine.

192
00:13:24,880 --> 00:13:25,500
Take your time.

193
00:13:25,500 --> 00:13:25,560
Take your time.

194
00:13:25,560 --> 00:13:25,620
Take your time.

195
00:13:33,320 --> 00:13:35,460
There are things I want to tell Kazehaya.

196
00:13:36,120 --> 00:13:37,420
Things I want to convey.

197
00:13:38,020 --> 00:13:39,880
So, uh...

198
00:13:39,880 --> 00:13:41,340
Shoot, I must not...

199
00:13:41,340 --> 00:13:42,920
Once I thought about it,

200
00:13:43,340 --> 00:13:45,600
there was a lot I wanted to tell him.

201
00:13:46,500 --> 00:13:48,580
But I didn't know how to put into words.

202
00:13:49,460 --> 00:13:50,440
Or where to start.

203
00:13:51,540 --> 00:13:53,720
I really wish...

204
00:13:53,720 --> 00:13:56,260
There was just a single word...

205
00:13:56,260 --> 00:13:57,420
To convey everything.

206
00:13:57,420 --> 00:14:08,080
And sent.

207
00:14:09,740 --> 00:14:11,160
To be honest...

208
00:14:11,160 --> 00:14:13,640
I was regretting not asking for your number before this.

209
00:14:14,180 --> 00:14:15,000
But just a bit.

210
00:14:16,220 --> 00:14:18,040
Maybe more than a bit.

211
00:14:21,040 --> 00:14:23,860
I kept thinking about how I should have asked much sooner.

212
00:14:23,860 --> 00:14:27,620
Oh, got it.

213
00:14:43,040 --> 00:14:44,420
Sawako, not Sadako.

214
00:14:45,100 --> 00:14:46,200
One, two, three, one.

215
00:14:47,900 --> 00:14:49,200
It goes back to one.

216
00:14:49,200 --> 00:14:55,960
Your birthday's...

217
00:14:55,960 --> 00:14:56,180
When?

218
00:15:00,180 --> 00:15:01,180
Today?

219
00:15:19,200 --> 00:15:25,640
Oh, there's only 15 more minutes left in a day.

220
00:15:26,920 --> 00:15:28,980
Oh, I guess you're right.

221
00:15:31,080 --> 00:15:32,320
Barely enough time.

222
00:15:33,660 --> 00:15:33,860
Huh?

223
00:15:38,500 --> 00:15:41,060
Happy birthday, Kuro Numa.

224
00:15:43,140 --> 00:15:44,940
Man, if I'd known sooner,

225
00:15:44,940 --> 00:15:47,140
I would have given you something.

226
00:15:49,200 --> 00:15:57,960
But...

227
00:15:57,960 --> 00:15:59,600
You already have.

228
00:16:00,240 --> 00:16:00,880
What?

229
00:16:01,560 --> 00:16:04,180
I got to see a side of you I didn't know yet.

230
00:16:05,180 --> 00:16:07,660
And saw you experience something new.

231
00:16:09,560 --> 00:16:10,200
Besides...

232
00:16:11,660 --> 00:16:13,780
This is actually the time

233
00:16:13,780 --> 00:16:15,460
that I was born.

234
00:16:15,460 --> 00:16:19,380
You were here, right by my side.

235
00:16:19,960 --> 00:16:21,220
The moment I turned 16.

236
00:16:26,220 --> 00:16:27,620
11.45 PM.

237
00:16:29,260 --> 00:16:30,560
I'm a year older.

238
00:16:31,760 --> 00:16:33,600
15 minutes...

239
00:16:33,600 --> 00:16:34,780
Until the new year.

240
00:16:34,780 --> 00:16:42,540
I'm curious.

241
00:16:42,540 --> 00:16:44,220
What kind of child were you?

242
00:16:45,280 --> 00:16:45,540
Huh?

243
00:16:45,880 --> 00:16:47,160
Well, uh...

244
00:16:47,160 --> 00:16:50,020
I don't think there was anything really special about me.

245
00:16:50,720 --> 00:16:51,300
Um...

246
00:16:51,300 --> 00:16:52,560
How do I put it?

247
00:16:53,180 --> 00:16:53,460
Huh.

248
00:16:53,720 --> 00:16:54,700
Then tell me an order.

249
00:16:56,160 --> 00:16:58,260
So you were born 16 years ago.

250
00:16:58,440 --> 00:16:58,780
And then?

251
00:16:59,140 --> 00:16:59,820
It's...

252
00:16:59,820 --> 00:17:00,680
gonna be boring.

253
00:17:01,120 --> 00:17:02,280
Don't worry about it.

254
00:17:02,500 --> 00:17:03,140
I don't care.

255
00:17:03,700 --> 00:17:05,100
I'm interested in your story.

256
00:17:06,360 --> 00:17:07,340
Go right ahead.

257
00:17:10,680 --> 00:17:12,480
Don't say I didn't warn you, okay?

258
00:17:12,480 --> 00:17:12,560
Okay?

259
00:17:15,240 --> 00:17:16,300
16 years ago,

260
00:17:16,640 --> 00:17:19,340
I was born weighing about 6 pounds.

261
00:17:19,980 --> 00:17:20,660
At age 4,

262
00:17:21,260 --> 00:17:22,160
I entered kindergarten.

263
00:17:22,900 --> 00:17:24,140
I was in Class Violet.

264
00:17:24,560 --> 00:17:25,320
Then Maybelle.

265
00:17:25,320 --> 00:17:26,080
Oh,

266
00:17:26,280 --> 00:17:28,740
this is where my cousin Eiji comes in.

267
00:17:29,140 --> 00:17:29,920
He used to call me

268
00:17:29,920 --> 00:17:31,580
Zashiki Warashi at that age.

269
00:17:31,960 --> 00:17:33,000
Zashiki Warashi?

270
00:17:33,520 --> 00:17:34,260
Bring me soda.

271
00:17:34,760 --> 00:17:35,520
I'm thirsty.

272
00:17:36,520 --> 00:17:36,960
Right away!

273
00:17:37,380 --> 00:17:40,060
I wonder if this story comes off as me bragging.

274
00:17:41,940 --> 00:17:43,880
In first grade and second grade,

275
00:17:44,140 --> 00:17:45,480
I was in Class Plum.

276
00:17:46,300 --> 00:17:47,300
Third and fourth?

277
00:17:47,820 --> 00:17:48,540
Class Pine.

278
00:17:49,080 --> 00:17:49,780
Fifth and sixth?

279
00:17:50,400 --> 00:17:51,280
Class Bamboo.

280
00:17:52,060 --> 00:17:53,160
Oh, Shoujiku Bai.

281
00:17:53,160 --> 00:17:55,400
What were your hobbies around then?

282
00:17:56,480 --> 00:17:57,000
Hobbies?

283
00:17:57,460 --> 00:17:58,320
Let's see.

284
00:18:00,820 --> 00:18:01,340
Oh!

285
00:18:01,680 --> 00:18:03,420
It was probably Solo Jump Rope.

286
00:18:03,520 --> 00:18:04,340
Solo what now?

287
00:18:04,720 --> 00:18:06,500
I would tie some elastic rope

288
00:18:06,500 --> 00:18:07,480
to a couple of chairs

289
00:18:07,480 --> 00:18:08,720
and jump all by myself.

290
00:18:09,340 --> 00:18:10,520
It was really fun.

291
00:18:11,520 --> 00:18:13,000
Well, for me anyway.

292
00:18:13,480 --> 00:18:14,560
I play things like

293
00:18:14,560 --> 00:18:15,860
Solo Volleyball too.

294
00:18:16,680 --> 00:18:17,940
Solo Cat's Cradle.

295
00:18:18,480 --> 00:18:20,120
Five Diamonds, Jacob's Ladder.

296
00:18:20,740 --> 00:18:21,900
Solo Speed also.

297
00:18:21,900 --> 00:18:23,800
It's way too fast!

298
00:18:24,620 --> 00:18:25,180
Solo!

299
00:18:27,060 --> 00:18:27,580
Wait.

300
00:18:28,880 --> 00:18:29,280
Ugh.

301
00:18:30,660 --> 00:18:31,780
Just forget it.

302
00:18:32,120 --> 00:18:33,500
I'm ruining the mood now.

303
00:18:34,200 --> 00:18:34,740
We're supposed to be celebrating...

304
00:18:34,740 --> 00:18:35,220
Stop it.

305
00:18:35,220 --> 00:18:36,760
You're doing no such thing.

306
00:18:36,760 --> 00:18:39,920
Well, if I'd heard that story

307
00:18:39,920 --> 00:18:41,360
at the beginning of the school year,

308
00:18:42,160 --> 00:18:44,420
I might have assumed

309
00:18:44,420 --> 00:18:45,660
that you liked being alone.

310
00:18:46,400 --> 00:18:48,400
But after we started talking

311
00:18:48,400 --> 00:18:49,940
and I got to know you,

312
00:18:50,300 --> 00:18:51,880
I realized you seem to enjoy

313
00:18:51,880 --> 00:18:52,700
anything you do.

314
00:18:53,980 --> 00:18:55,580
So I had this image of you

315
00:18:55,580 --> 00:18:56,820
finding fun in everything.

316
00:18:56,820 --> 00:18:58,820
Huh?

317
00:18:59,160 --> 00:19:00,360
And thinking about it

318
00:19:00,360 --> 00:19:01,400
makes me happy.

319
00:19:02,980 --> 00:19:03,860
So then,

320
00:19:04,060 --> 00:19:05,380
is that...

321
00:19:05,380 --> 00:19:07,340
Okaze Hai has always seen me?

322
00:19:08,300 --> 00:19:09,160
And the rest?

323
00:19:09,540 --> 00:19:09,820
Uh...

324
00:19:10,420 --> 00:19:10,820
Well...

325
00:19:11,540 --> 00:19:13,660
I entered middle school

326
00:19:13,660 --> 00:19:14,860
when I was around 12.

327
00:19:15,420 --> 00:19:17,440
Oh, elementary school went fast.

328
00:19:18,160 --> 00:19:18,600
Well,

329
00:19:18,840 --> 00:19:20,440
nothing special really happened.

330
00:19:20,440 --> 00:19:22,720
But then in my third year,

331
00:19:23,100 --> 00:19:24,720
Kitahoro Hai near my house

332
00:19:24,720 --> 00:19:26,440
was holding entrance exams.

333
00:19:30,280 --> 00:19:31,700
At 15,

334
00:19:32,160 --> 00:19:33,080
in spring,

335
00:19:34,080 --> 00:19:36,420
I met you.

336
00:19:40,080 --> 00:19:41,200
I thought,

337
00:19:41,540 --> 00:19:43,620
if I could become like Kaze Haya,

338
00:19:46,020 --> 00:19:47,440
maybe...

339
00:19:47,440 --> 00:19:51,040
that could help me grow

340
00:19:51,040 --> 00:19:52,000
and change?

341
00:19:57,780 --> 00:19:58,680
Thanks a lot.

342
00:20:15,000 --> 00:20:16,860
It was always Kaze Haya.

343
00:20:17,440 --> 00:20:19,740
who inspired change in me.

344
00:20:29,160 --> 00:20:30,980
This year was so different

345
00:20:30,980 --> 00:20:33,200
from all the years before.

346
00:20:34,480 --> 00:20:36,000
But that part of the story

347
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:38,160
would take too long.

348
00:20:38,160 --> 00:20:56,480
A special year

349
00:20:56,480 --> 00:20:58,260
where I was able to stay

350
00:20:58,260 --> 00:20:59,460
beside Kaze Haya.

351
00:20:59,460 --> 00:21:02,240
and now the birthday

352
00:21:02,240 --> 00:21:03,120
we spent together

353
00:21:03,120 --> 00:21:03,740
is ending.

354
00:21:05,740 --> 00:21:06,200
However,

355
00:21:07,200 --> 00:21:08,280
a brand new year

356
00:21:08,280 --> 00:21:10,400
is about to begin.

357
00:21:10,400 --> 00:21:11,400
And it was très long.

358
00:21:11,400 --> 00:21:41,380
I'll see you next time.

359
00:21:41,400 --> 00:22:11,380
I'll see you next time.

360
00:22:11,400 --> 00:22:41,380
I'll see you next time.

361
00:22:41,400 --> 00:23:11,380
I'll see you next time.

